{"reference":"Isaiah 49","book":"Isaiah","chapter":49,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Who Is the Servant?","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The servant in verses 1–7 speaks as one called and formed for a task, yet verse 3 names the servant “Israel,” while verses 5–6 describe the servant’s work as bringing Jacob and Israel back. Isaiah uses several voices and forms of address, so the speaker should be identified from the passage itself rather than assumed in advance. The singular servant language has been read in different ways—as individual, collective, prophetic, royal, or messianic—and the chapter does not by itself settle every later interpretive question. It is also important to distinguish what the passage says in its own setting from later quotations, allusions, and religious readings of it.","verse_refs":["Isaiah 49:1-7","Isaiah 49:14-26"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_isaiah_049_03c7336ce2b62a36e5d3734f"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Isaiah as a Book","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"Isaiah 49 belongs to a larger book preserved in several ancient manuscript witnesses. The Great Isaiah Scroll is an almost complete copy of all sixty-six chapters. It broadly aligns with the Masoretic tradition, while also containing many spelling and some substantive differences; other Qumran manuscripts and interpretive writings show that Isaiah was actively copied and interpreted.","verse_refs":["Isaiah 10:1-34","Isaiah 11:1-16","Isaiah 12:1-6","Isaiah 13:1-22","Isaiah 14:1-32","Isaiah 15:1-9","Isaiah 16:1-14","Isaiah 17:1-14","Isaiah 18:1-7","Isaiah 19:1-25","Isaiah 1:1-31","Isaiah 20:1-6","Isaiah 21:1-17","Isaiah 22:1-25","Isaiah 23:1-18","Isaiah 24:1-23","Isaiah 25:1-12","Isaiah 26:1-21","Isaiah 27:1-13","Isaiah 28:1-29","Isaiah 29:1-24","Isaiah 2:1-22","Isaiah 30:1-33","Isaiah 31:1-9","Isaiah 32:1-20","Isaiah 33:1-24","Isaiah 34:1-17","Isaiah 35:1-10","Isaiah 36:1-22","Isaiah 37:1-38","Isaiah 38:1-22","Isaiah 39:1-8","Isaiah 3:1-26","Isaiah 40:1-31","Isaiah 41:1-29","Isaiah 42:1-25","Isaiah 43:1-28","Isaiah 44:1-28","Isaiah 45:1-25","Isaiah 46:1-13","Isaiah 47:1-15","Isaiah 48:1-22","Isaiah 4:1-6","Isaiah 50:1-11","Isaiah 51:1-23","Isaiah 52:1-15","Isaiah 53:1-12","Isaiah 54:1-17","Isaiah 55:1-13","Isaiah 56:1-12","Isaiah 57:1-21","Isaiah 58:1-14","Isaiah 59:1-21","Isaiah 5:1-30","Isaiah 60:1-22","Isaiah 61:1-11","Isaiah 62:1-12","Isaiah 63:1-19","Isaiah 64:1-12","Isaiah 65:1-25","Isaiah 66:1-24","Isaiah 6:1-13","Isaiah 7:1-25","Isaiah 8:1-22","Isaiah 9:1-21"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_isaiah_049_e0fcc2cdd0baca1505a117ed"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}